1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:01,600
<i> Mom, have you seen Peter?</i>

2
00:00:01,833 --> 00:00:03,467
<i>I am here at the warehouse
to warn Jin Ho.</i>

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,633
<i> Peter, come on!</i>

4
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:05,733
<i> Where is this going?</i>

5
00:00:05,867 --> 00:00:06,700
<i> What are you doing here?</i>

6
00:00:06,833 --> 00:00:07,867
<i>We just need to leave.
Now!</i>

7
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,467
<i> I need you to get out of here.</i>

8
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,400
<i> Why is there no one here?</i>

9
00:00:10,533 --> 00:00:12,033
<i> You have nowhere left to run!</i>

10
00:00:12,167 --> 00:00:13,167
<i> This is an ambush!</i>

11
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:14,367
<i> You look pretty happy.</i>

12
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:15,700
<i> I just had a big win today.</i>

13
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:17,100
<i> You knew they were coming!</i>

14
00:00:17,233 --> 00:00:18,367
<i> Because you led them here!</i>

15
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,800
<i>My father. I need to get to him!</i>

16
00:00:19,933 --> 00:00:21,700
<i>You are really going to charge
into the middle of a shootout?</i>

17
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:23,433
<i>I am not leaving
while my father is in there</i>

18
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:24,500
<i> fighting for his life!</i>

19
00:00:24,633 --> 00:00:25,600
<i> Stop!</i>

20
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:27,600
<i>None of you are getting out
of here alive!</i>

21
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:29,167
<i> I do not want to die yet.</i>

22
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:30,667
<i> We need backup now!</i>

23
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:36,433
<i> [OBB]</i>

24
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:52,433
[GUN FIRING IN DISTANCE]

25
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:56,533
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

26
00:00:57,267 --> 00:00:58,667
Stop!

27
00:01:01,067 --> 00:01:02,133
Kill them!

28
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:07,500
[GUN FIRING]
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

29
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:12,800
[GUN FIRING]

30
00:01:13,667 --> 00:01:17,133
[GUN FIRING]

31
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:22,333
[GUN FIRING]

32
00:01:25,633 --> 00:01:28,033
[GUN FIRING]

33
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:31,733
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

34
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:37,933
Joey...

35
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:39,600
[GUN FIRING IN DISTANCE]

36
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:41,267
Jin Ho...

37
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:43,567
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:01:43,700 --> 00:01:44,900
What are you doing here?

39
00:01:45,033 --> 00:01:47,267
Jin Ho, I cannot blame you
if you are angry with us.

40
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:53,300
But I heard you let
Peter escape.

41
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:55,767
So, that means you are
still on our side, right?

42
00:01:57,833 --> 00:01:59,800
Jin Ho, please help me.

43
00:02:00,933 --> 00:02:02,800
I need to get my father out.

44
00:02:02,933 --> 00:02:05,367
I need to make sure he is alive.

45
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:07,067
I saw him.

46
00:02:08,133 --> 00:02:09,967
He is alive.

47
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:11,967
Jin Ho, please help me.

48
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:13,900
We need to get my father out.
Please!

49
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:15,467
Help me.

50
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,400
Why should I?

51
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:22,400
You're lucky I haven't shot you.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:25,933
You used me to get Liza!

53
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:28,567
Jin Ho, I know what they did

54
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:29,933
to my family.

55
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:32,367
I just want all of this to end.

56
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:35,600
And you want the same thing too,
don't you?

57
00:02:35,733 --> 00:02:37,533
You used us to get to Liza!

58
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:41,667
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,300
[GUN FIRING IN DISTANCE]

60
00:02:44,433 --> 00:02:46,100
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:47,767
Stop! Surrender now!

62
00:02:47,933 --> 00:02:49,333
[GUN FIRES]

63
00:02:52,533 --> 00:02:55,133
But I never put you in danger.

64
00:02:55,267 --> 00:02:58,033
I helped you and protected you

65
00:02:58,167 --> 00:03:00,400
while we were looking
for Liza together.

66
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:01,767
Maybe you were a true friend,

67
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:03,667
as much as you could be.

68
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,800
But I hope
you understand this too.

69
00:03:07,933 --> 00:03:10,267
I have a family to protect,
Jin Ho!

70
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,633
At my expense?

71
00:03:16,133 --> 00:03:18,667
I am sorry, Jin Ho.
I really am.

72
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,700
[GUN FIRING IN DISTANCE]

73
00:03:31,067 --> 00:03:33,233
- Hey!
- Hey! Stop!

74
00:03:33,367 --> 00:03:34,800
Hands up!

75
00:03:36,167 --> 00:03:37,433
Hands up!

76
00:03:37,567 --> 00:03:41,600
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

77
00:03:49,433 --> 00:03:51,700
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

78
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:52,967
Come on, hands up!

79
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:54,400
Hands up!

80
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,267
Arrest them!

81
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:01,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:19,567
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

83
00:04:24,167 --> 00:04:25,633
Jin Ho!

84
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:32,500
At long last...
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:04:33,367 --> 00:04:35,500
We finally meet, woman.

86
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:37,767
You are only brave
because you have a gun.

87
00:04:38,667 --> 00:04:41,433
Try fighting without it.

88
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,067
Go ahead.

89
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,000
Let us see how good
you really are.

90
00:04:47,967 --> 00:04:49,433
Liza...

91
00:04:52,133 --> 00:04:54,433
Do not interfere!

92
00:04:54,933 --> 00:04:57,267
Stay here.

93
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,767
[WHACKS]

94
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:05,500
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

95
00:05:05,633 --> 00:05:07,333
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:07,467 --> 00:05:08,700
[THUDS]

97
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:14,700
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

98
00:05:18,733 --> 00:05:21,300
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

99
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,933
[GRUNTING]

100
00:05:27,067 --> 00:05:31,267
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

101
00:05:36,333 --> 00:05:38,200
[GRUNTING]

102
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:41,567
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:05:43,067 --> 00:05:44,467
[THUDS]

104
00:05:49,567 --> 00:05:53,667
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

105
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,067
Okay.

106
00:06:01,367 --> 00:06:03,133
You have proven
that you are skilled.

107
00:06:04,033 --> 00:06:06,233
But you know,
I realized something...

108
00:06:06,367 --> 00:06:10,067
I am not here to compete
or prove myself.

109
00:06:10,633 --> 00:06:13,200
I am here to kill you!

110
00:06:14,067 --> 00:06:15,800
I have an idea.

111
00:06:18,167 --> 00:06:20,300
Do the honors, Jin Ho.

112
00:06:20,433 --> 00:06:22,167
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:24,467
I will give you
the revenge you want.

114
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:27,767
Did she not betray you?

115
00:06:28,267 --> 00:06:30,067
You understand that, right?

116
00:06:31,033 --> 00:06:32,500
So do it!

117
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,100
This is your last chance
to prove your loyalty.

118
00:06:36,233 --> 00:06:40,433
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:06:41,667 --> 00:06:43,133
Do it!

120
00:06:43,267 --> 00:06:46,433
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

121
00:06:56,733 --> 00:06:58,733
Do it now!

122
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,700
What are you waiting for?

123
00:07:02,833 --> 00:07:04,733
Jin Ho, do not.
Please.

124
00:07:06,033 --> 00:07:07,633
You...

125
00:07:07,767 --> 00:07:11,767
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

126
00:07:12,933 --> 00:07:14,600
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

127
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,733
You betrayed me, Joey.

128
00:07:21,633 --> 00:07:23,633
So, that is your real name.

129
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:28,867
Have a safe trip to hell, Joey.

130
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:32,900
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:07:33,433 --> 00:07:35,533
The gunfire inside has stopped.

132
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:39,500
The police and DDE agents
may have finished it.

133
00:07:39,633 --> 00:07:41,600
Hopefully, everyone
is being arrested now.

134
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:44,733
But, Joey...

135
00:07:44,867 --> 00:07:46,700
we need to find her now.

136
00:07:47,867 --> 00:07:49,733
Jin Ho, do it now!

137
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:54,633
I just wanted to give
that to you

138
00:07:54,767 --> 00:07:56,267
so that wherever you are,

139
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,633
no matter where you go,

140
00:07:57,767 --> 00:07:59,567
you will never forget
that you have friends.

141
00:07:59,700 --> 00:08:00,967
You have us.

142
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,900
[CHUCKLES]

143
00:08:03,033 --> 00:08:05,167
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:07,067
If you won't do it...

145
00:08:08,933 --> 00:08:10,900
then I will.

146
00:08:15,967 --> 00:08:19,033
- [GUN FIRING]
- [LIZA GROANING]

147
00:08:19,167 --> 00:08:20,400
Let's go! Let's go!

148
00:08:20,533 --> 00:08:22,433
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

149
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:25,400
[GROANING]
Traitors!

150
00:08:26,467 --> 00:08:29,600
[GUN FIRING]

151
00:08:32,433 --> 00:08:33,567
We have to leave now.

152
00:08:33,700 --> 00:08:34,533
What?

153
00:08:34,667 --> 00:08:35,700
When I count to three...

154
00:08:35,833 --> 00:08:36,700
This is my car.

155
00:08:36,833 --> 00:08:38,200
- You run, okay?
- Jin Ho, it is dangerous!

156
00:08:38,333 --> 00:08:42,067
One, two, three!

157
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,200
Run!

158
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:47,067
[GUN FIRING]
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,833
Andrew and Peter!

160
00:08:48,967 --> 00:08:52,167
[GUN FIRING]

161
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:56,000
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

162
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,667
[GUN FIRING]

163
00:09:05,667 --> 00:09:07,033
What about Andrew and Peter?

164
00:09:07,167 --> 00:09:09,033
Do not worry about them!
We need to go!

165
00:09:09,167 --> 00:09:09,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

166
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:13,033
[GUN FIRING]

167
00:09:13,167 --> 00:09:14,667
[GROANS]

168
00:09:15,667 --> 00:09:19,767
[POLICE SIREN WAILING
IN DISTANCE]

169
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:23,800
Come on, let's go!

170
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,233
Let's go! Come on!

171
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,067
[GUN FIRING]

172
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:33,367
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:45,267
Zoey, just hold on.
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

174
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,800
I thought I was going to die,
Sir.

175
00:09:47,933 --> 00:09:49,900
There are still so many things
I want to do.

176
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:52,400
I want to be with
the person I love.

177
00:09:52,533 --> 00:09:54,633
Zoey, you will do all of that

178
00:09:54,767 --> 00:09:56,600
because you are going to live.

179
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,233
The DDE still needs you.

180
00:10:00,367 --> 00:10:01,800
And besides,

181
00:10:01,967 --> 00:10:04,467
we still have to take down
the syndicate, right?

182
00:10:06,700 --> 00:10:08,667
Sir, we need to move her now.

183
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:10,200
All right.

184
00:10:10,333 --> 00:10:14,433
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

185
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:27,133
So, it was definitely an ambush.

186
00:10:27,267 --> 00:10:29,300
They waited for all of us
to gather inside

187
00:10:29,433 --> 00:10:31,067
before opening fire.

188
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:33,200
It was as if they knew a warrant
was about to be served.

189
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:35,033
They planned this in advance.

190
00:10:35,467 --> 00:10:36,400
Sir, we have bad news.

191
00:10:36,533 --> 00:10:38,400
Liza and Jin Ho escaped.

192
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,133
Have you alerted
the nearby stations?

193
00:10:41,267 --> 00:10:43,033
Put out an alert...

194
00:10:43,167 --> 00:10:44,400
with their vehicle descriptions.

195
00:10:44,533 --> 00:10:46,167
We have already done that, Sir.

196
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:48,000
Good.

197
00:10:49,867 --> 00:10:54,000
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

198
00:10:56,967 --> 00:10:58,967
Andrew, I am asking you.

199
00:10:59,800 --> 00:11:02,000
Do not report this
to your podcast yet.

200
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:04,933
Major, I am not here
to cover anything up.

201
00:11:05,067 --> 00:11:06,933
I came here for Joey.

202
00:11:07,333 --> 00:11:08,900
Joey?

203
00:11:09,067 --> 00:11:10,233
Why?

204
00:11:10,367 --> 00:11:12,600
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

205
00:11:12,733 --> 00:11:14,867
Jin Ho took him, Major.

206
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,233
What?

207
00:11:17,367 --> 00:11:21,433
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,600
[FROG CROAKING]

209
00:11:31,733 --> 00:11:34,200
Ah, Jin Ho...

210
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,233
where are we now?

211
00:11:35,367 --> 00:11:36,933
Why does it feel like
we are so far away?

212
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:40,767
There is not even any signal.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

213
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:44,567
About a hundred kilometers
from the warehouse.

214
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:48,767
Yes, it is far,
which means we are safe.

215
00:11:51,667 --> 00:11:53,933
Are you sure this is safe?

216
00:11:54,067 --> 00:11:56,367
It feels like we are
in a haunted forest.

217
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:57,767
Then you choose.

218
00:11:57,900 --> 00:12:00,000
Death or Liza.

219
00:12:00,133 --> 00:12:02,467
She is not finished with us yet,
Joey.

220
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,633
She will look for us.

221
00:12:03,767 --> 00:12:06,567
So, we have to stay away
for a while.

222
00:12:08,433 --> 00:12:10,033
For a while?

223
00:12:11,433 --> 00:12:13,233
How long, Jin Ho?

224
00:12:13,367 --> 00:12:14,700
Because...

225
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:17,500
of course, I need
to check on my father.

226
00:12:17,633 --> 00:12:20,300
They need to know
that I am safe.

227
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,233
I will just try
to find a signal.

228
00:12:26,933 --> 00:12:27,967
Go ahead.

229
00:12:28,100 --> 00:12:31,267
If you can make it through
the darkness, go ahead.

230
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:35,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

231
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:44,567
[SIGHS]

232
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:48,900
- [FROG CROAKING]
- [GECKO VOCALIZING]

233
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:53,067
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:12:58,467 --> 00:13:00,667
[LOW BATTERY PROMPT CHIMES]

235
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:04,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

236
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:09,133
- [FROG CROAKING]
- [GECKO VOCALIZING]

237
00:13:09,267 --> 00:13:14,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:20,133
I thought you were leaving?

239
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,067
My phone battery died.

240
00:13:24,767 --> 00:13:26,700
Just go with me, okay?

241
00:13:27,167 --> 00:13:28,067
I will open the gate.

242
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,667
Just stay here.

243
00:13:30,333 --> 00:13:32,800
There might be monsters here,
you know.

244
00:13:33,800 --> 00:13:36,867
Monsters are usually eat
the noisy ones.

245
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:41,067
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

246
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:53,100
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:54,767
Come on.

248
00:13:54,933 --> 00:13:58,167
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

249
00:14:07,933 --> 00:14:09,567
[GUN COCKS]

250
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:13,733
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

251
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,200
Ah, Jin Ho...

252
00:14:17,333 --> 00:14:19,300
Where exactly are we?

253
00:14:20,633 --> 00:14:23,033
This is my last safe house.

254
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,600
Only people I trust
know about this.

255
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:33,600
So, we will just hide here?

256
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:38,667
Why do we not just report this
to my father?

257
00:14:41,667 --> 00:14:43,567
Do you think Liza will give up

258
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,933
just because you told
the police?

259
00:14:46,067 --> 00:14:48,233
She's really mad at you,

260
00:14:48,367 --> 00:14:50,933
and me for helping you.

261
00:14:52,700 --> 00:14:56,033
When she finds us,
she will kill us.

262
00:14:57,300 --> 00:15:00,367
So, unless you want us both
buried tonight,

263
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:03,267
this is the safest place
we have.

264
00:15:03,433 --> 00:15:07,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

265
00:15:10,067 --> 00:15:11,633
Oh, by the way, Jin Ho...

266
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:17,767
Why did you shoot Liza
instead of me?

267
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:21,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:24,433
Damn that Jin Ho!
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

269
00:15:24,567 --> 00:15:25,433
I could not chase after him

270
00:15:25,567 --> 00:15:27,233
because the police
had already arrived!

271
00:15:27,667 --> 00:15:29,300
[GROANING]

272
00:15:29,433 --> 00:15:32,800
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

273
00:15:35,633 --> 00:15:37,267
- You said...
- [GROANING]

274
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,400
your plan was solid.

275
00:15:39,833 --> 00:15:41,200
- You said...
- [GROANING]

276
00:15:41,333 --> 00:15:43,267
you will handle it!

277
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:45,133
- You said...
- [GROANING]

278
00:15:45,267 --> 00:15:48,433
You said that Jin Ho
would not betray us!

279
00:15:48,567 --> 00:15:49,967
Look what happened!

280
00:15:50,100 --> 00:15:52,367
You brought us a liability!

281
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:55,400
[GROANING]

282
00:15:56,900 --> 00:15:58,833
Clean this mess up,

283
00:15:58,967 --> 00:16:02,867
or next time, you will get more
than that from me.

284
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,967
Stand up.

285
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,533
[GROANS]

286
00:16:09,700 --> 00:16:13,533
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

287
00:16:14,100 --> 00:16:16,300
[GROANS]

288
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:19,267
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

289
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,200
Why did you shoot Liza
instead of me?

290
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,067
[SIGHS]

291
00:16:31,533 --> 00:16:34,133
I do not know, okay?

292
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:35,933
I do not even know
if I made the right choice.

293
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:38,667
You might turn me over
to the police in the end.

294
00:16:39,867 --> 00:16:40,900
Jin Ho, if I wanted to do that,

295
00:16:41,033 --> 00:16:42,767
I would have done it earlier.

296
00:16:42,933 --> 00:16:46,333
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

297
00:16:46,467 --> 00:16:48,833
I know you and Liza
have a history.

298
00:16:49,867 --> 00:16:52,667
You even used us to find her,
right?

299
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:56,633
You just wanted to find her,

300
00:16:56,767 --> 00:16:58,633
not to arrest her.

301
00:16:59,533 --> 00:17:01,300
That is why I want to ask...

302
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:05,500
What happened?
Why did you break away from her?

303
00:17:05,633 --> 00:17:09,833
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

304
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:16,533
You want to talk
to your parents?

305
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:18,033
I have a way.

306
00:17:21,767 --> 00:17:23,267
Why did he take Joey?

307
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,333
What does he need from her?

308
00:17:26,367 --> 00:17:29,167
Miguel, he might do something
to Joey.

309
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:31,233
Clarissa, they are tracing

310
00:17:31,367 --> 00:17:33,400
the route of Jin Ho's vehicle.

311
00:17:35,067 --> 00:17:36,933
Auntie Clarissa,
please do not be afraid.

312
00:17:37,067 --> 00:17:38,700
Jin Ho is not a bad person.

313
00:17:38,833 --> 00:17:41,000
I am sure he will not hurt Joey.

314
00:17:41,133 --> 00:17:43,067
We cannot be sure about that,
Peter.

315
00:17:43,200 --> 00:17:44,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

316
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,700
Jin Ho is a member
of the syndicate,

317
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:47,700
and that syndicate

318
00:17:47,833 --> 00:17:50,200
has been looking for Joey
for a long time.

319
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:52,300
But Jin Ho went against them,
right?

320
00:17:52,433 --> 00:17:54,833
We saw that earlier ourselves.

321
00:17:55,333 --> 00:17:57,267
Maybe he is just saving Joey.

322
00:17:57,800 --> 00:17:59,200
Saving her?

323
00:17:59,333 --> 00:18:00,767
If he is saving her,

324
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:02,600
why can we still
not contact her?

325
00:18:02,733 --> 00:18:06,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

326
00:18:16,100 --> 00:18:18,700
Here, you can call your father.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

327
00:18:19,433 --> 00:18:21,733
Tell him that you are okay.

328
00:18:22,333 --> 00:18:23,567
Okay.

329
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:25,500
But...

330
00:18:25,967 --> 00:18:28,200
you cannot tell where you are,

331
00:18:28,333 --> 00:18:29,700
and keep it short.

332
00:18:29,833 --> 00:18:30,967
They might trace the call.

333
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:34,567
If they do, it could lead Liza
straight to us.

334
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,400
Are we clear?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

335
00:18:37,167 --> 00:18:39,233
- Clear.
- Good.

336
00:18:40,033 --> 00:18:41,800
I saved you, Joey.

337
00:18:41,933 --> 00:18:44,433
Prove to me that I made
the right choice.

338
00:18:44,567 --> 00:18:48,833
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

339
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:55,667
[PHONE KEYS BEEPING]

340
00:18:55,833 --> 00:18:59,300
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

341
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:03,500
[PHONE RINGING]

342
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:08,233
[PHONE RINGING]

343
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:10,267
Hello?

344
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:12,333
Hello, Dad?

345
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:13,733
Joey?

346
00:19:13,867 --> 00:19:15,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

347
00:19:15,167 --> 00:19:16,467
Joey!

348
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:19,167
Dad, are you okay?

349
00:19:20,133 --> 00:19:22,100
I am at home.
I am here with your mother.

350
00:19:22,233 --> 00:19:24,300
- Where are you?
- Joey, my child!

351
00:19:24,433 --> 00:19:26,500
<i> Joey, my child, where are you?</i>

352
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:29,000
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:19:32,567 --> 00:19:37,967
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

354
00:19:44,967 --> 00:19:47,300
Ah, I am okay.

355
00:19:48,600 --> 00:19:51,067
<i>I am safe.
Please do not worry.</i>

356
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:53,767
Joey, why did you go
with Jin Ho?

357
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:56,600
<i>Please tell us
where you are right now.</i>

358
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:58,133
Yes...

359
00:19:59,033 --> 00:20:03,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

360
00:20:03,167 --> 00:20:04,567
- Joey!
- Joey!

361
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:06,067
Joey!

362
00:20:06,667 --> 00:20:08,233
The call was cut.

363
00:20:08,367 --> 00:20:09,567
That is enough.

364
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:10,667
Okay.

365
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:12,433
Thank you.

366
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:14,267
Did I not tell you

367
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,433
that we have nothing to fear?

368
00:20:16,567 --> 00:20:18,533
Joey is with Jin Ho.

369
00:20:18,667 --> 00:20:19,667
He did not hurt her.

370
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,400
She is safe.

371
00:20:21,533 --> 00:20:23,100
The things Joey was saying

372
00:20:23,233 --> 00:20:24,933
are the exact same lines

373
00:20:25,067 --> 00:20:27,700
used by kidnapping victims.

374
00:20:27,833 --> 00:20:29,633
We cannot afford
to be complacent.

375
00:20:29,767 --> 00:20:33,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

376
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:43,567
You were the one asking, right?

377
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:44,567
And she answered.

378
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,267
You heard her,
she was not crying.

379
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:47,433
Her voice was steady.

380
00:20:47,567 --> 00:20:48,333
She did not sound afraid.

381
00:20:48,467 --> 00:20:49,867
What are you talking about?

382
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,967
Which proves my point.

383
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:54,533
It is obvious
that someone was watching Joey.

384
00:21:01,733 --> 00:21:04,700
Peter, what you are saying
is hard to believe,

385
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:07,133
and I do not trust
that Korean man.

386
00:21:08,467 --> 00:21:10,933
Clarissa, I will not stop

387
00:21:11,067 --> 00:21:13,167
until I find Joey.

388
00:21:13,867 --> 00:21:15,167
That is a promise.

389
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:19,333
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

390
00:21:28,867 --> 00:21:33,167
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:21:36,833 --> 00:21:38,500
I do not know
what condition she was in

392
00:21:38,633 --> 00:21:39,600
when we got caught in the chaos.

393
00:21:39,733 --> 00:21:41,767
Then the Korean syndicate
took him.

394
00:21:41,900 --> 00:21:43,467
Do not move.

395
00:21:43,633 --> 00:21:44,733
They got a lead.

396
00:21:44,867 --> 00:21:47,333
They spotted Jin Ho's vehicle
on a toll camera.

397
00:21:47,467 --> 00:21:48,433
Uncle, which toll gate?

398
00:21:48,567 --> 00:21:49,567
At Sta. Monica.

399
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,400
Find Jin Ho as fast as you can.

400
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:53,600
The police are already moving
to find them.

401
00:21:53,733 --> 00:21:55,367
We need to get to them first

402
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:57,900
because Jin Ho
will definitely give us up.

403
00:21:58,033 --> 00:21:59,567
Remember, he saw me.

404
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,833
I am sorry, brother-in-law.

405
00:22:00,967 --> 00:22:04,200
Instead of saving them, it looks
like you made things worse.

406
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,233
Jin Ho!
Jin Ho...
